Source: Debian cairo 1.18.6-1 (sid), debian/patches/image-info-Fix-out-of-bounds-read-and-uninitialized-info-.patch

From: Ana Bobillo <anabobillo3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:17:25 +0200
Subject: image-info: Fix out-of-bounds read and uninitialized info for JPEG

At a start of frame marker, _cairo_image_info_get_jpeg_info() checks
that p[0] to p[7] are within the data, where p points to the second
byte of the marker, but _jpeg_extract_info() also reads p[8], the
number of components. Check that p[8] is within the data.

If the data ends without a start of frame segment, the function
returned success without setting any field of info. The PDF, PS, SVG
and win32 printing surfaces then used the uninitialized width, height
and number of components. Return CAIRO_INT_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED instead,
so that the image is embedded as if it had no JPEG mime data.

Also make _jpeg_skip_segment() return the end of the data instead of a
pointer beyond it when the segment length is larger than the remaining
data.

(cherry picked from commit dd4da532e5a25935b08f5324a44b35246aa743e8)

Origin: upstream, after 1.18.6
---
 src/cairo-image-info.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cairo-image-info.c b/src/cairo-image-info.c
index 9693e48..bdfee4e 100644
--- a/src/cairo-image-info.c
+++ b/src/cairo-image-info.c
@@ -68,13 +68,16 @@
 #define SOF15 0xcf
 
 static const unsigned char *
-_jpeg_skip_segment (const unsigned char *p)
+_jpeg_skip_segment (const unsigned char *p, const unsigned char *end)
 {
     int len;
 
     p++;
     len = (p[0] << 8) | p[1];
 
+    if (len > end - p)
+	return end;
+
     return p + len;
 }
 
@@ -125,7 +128,7 @@ _cairo_image_info_get_jpeg_info (cairo_image_info_t	*info,
 	case SOF14:
 	case SOF15:
 	    /* Start of frame found. Extract the image parameters. */
-	    if (p + 8 > data + length)
+	    if (p + 9 > data + length)
 		return CAIRO_INT_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED;
 
 	    _jpeg_extract_info (info, p);
@@ -140,12 +143,13 @@ _cairo_image_info_get_jpeg_info (cairo_image_info_t	*info,
 	    if (p + 3 > data + length)
 		return CAIRO_INT_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED;
 
-	    p = _jpeg_skip_segment (p);
+	    p = _jpeg_skip_segment (p, data + length);
 	    break;
 	}
     }
 
-    return CAIRO_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    /* No start of frame found. */
+    return CAIRO_INT_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED;
 }
 
 /* JPEG 2000 (image/jp2)
